      "description": "The fixed status sign: diamond + word + one colour.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-sign ds-sign-alert\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10 2.8 17.2 10 10 17.2 2.8 10Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg>Discrepancy</span> <span class=\"ds-sign\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"7.2\"/><path d=\"M7.9 7.9a2.2 2.2 0 1 1 3 2.1c-.6.3-.9.8-.9 1.4v.3\"/></svg>Needs human review</span>",
      "css": ".ds-sign{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font:700 0.875rem/1.5 var(--font,system-ui);color:var(--ink,#1b2326);white-space:nowrap}.ds-sign-alert{color:var(--alert,#b2390d)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Finding Sign Plate",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "plate-alert",
      "description": "A finding: sign, record vs document values, and evidence rows that jump to their quote.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-plate ds-plate-alert\"><span class=\"ds-sign ds-sign-alert\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10 2.8 17.2 10 10 17.2 2.8 10Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg>Discrepancy</span><div class=\"ds-plate-field\">Maximum ICANS grade</div><button class=\"ds-ev\"><span class=\"ds-ev-ref\">Progress note, Day +6</span><span class=\"ds-ev-quote\">quoted source text</span></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-plate{display:grid;gap:8px;border:1px solid var(--line,#dbe2e3);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;background:var(--surface,#fff);font-family:var(--font,system-ui);color:var(--ink,#1b2326)}.ds-plate-alert{border-color:var(--alert-line,#ecc2ab);background:var(--alert-soft,#fcefe8)}.ds-sign{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-weight:700;font-size:0.875rem}.ds-sign-alert{color:var(--alert,#b2390d)}.ds-plate-field{font-weight:700}.ds-ev{display:grid;gap:1px;text-align:left;border:0;background:transparent;border-radius:6px;padding:5px 8px;margin:0 -8px;cursor:pointer;font:inherit;transition:transform 150ms cubic-bezier(0.23,1,0.32,1)}.ds-ev:hover,.ds-ev:focus-visible{background:var(--accent-soft,#e1f0f2)}.ds-ev:active{transform:scale(0.99)}.ds-ev-ref{font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--ink-2,#4c5a61)}.ds-ev-quote{font-size:0.875rem}.ds-ev-quote::before{content:'\\201C'}.ds-ev-quote::after{content:'\\201D'}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Decision Choice",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "accent-soft",
      "description": "Review decision options; the checked one lights teal.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-choices\"><label class=\"ds-choice\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"d\" checked>Confirm discrepancy</label><label class=\"ds-choice\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"d\">Dismiss</label><label class=\"ds-choice\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"d\">Needs clinician</label></div>",
      "css": ".ds-choices{display:flex;gap:8px;font-family:var(--font,system-ui)}.ds-choice{position:relative;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong,#b8c5c8);border-radius:6px;padding:7px 14px;cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;background:var(--surface,#fff);transition:background-color 150ms ease,border-color 150ms ease,transform 150ms cubic-bezier(0.23,1,0.32,1)}.ds-choice:active{transform:scale(0.97)}.ds-choice input{position:absolute;opacity:0}.ds-choice:has(input:checked){border-color:var(--accent,#146a78);background:var(--accent-soft,#e1f0f2);color:var(--accent-text,#11606d)}.ds-choice:has(input:focus-visible){outline:2px solid var(--focus,#146a78);outline-offset:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Hospital Signpost",
    "overview": "ReSauce looks like the wayfinding of a well-run hospital: a deep petrol sign panel down the left, a calm cool-grey corridor behind the work, and white boards where the reading happens. Every status is a fixed sign made of one symbol, one word and at most one colour, so a reviewer who has been at the desk for hours, or watching on a projector, always knows where they are and what is waiting for them.\n\nDensity is that of a working tool, not a dashboard: tables, document text and finding plates sit close together, and hierarchy comes from type size, weight and a 68ch reading measure rather than from nested boxes. Colour is scarce on purpose. Teal means \"you can act here\" or \"this is selected\"; orange-red means \"discrepancy\" and never appears without its diamond and its word. Everything else is ink on neutral. The light and dark themes share one token set (`web/src/styles.css`, `:root` plus the dark overrides), toggled by `data-theme` or the system preference.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Petrol sign-panel sidebar with white legends; neutral ground; white work surfaces.",
      "One action accent, one discrepancy signal, nothing else saturated.",
      "A fixed status vocabulary (the sign) reused in every table, queue and plate.",
      "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next for words, IBM Plex Mono for IDs, dates and offsets; tabular figures everywhere.",
      "One motion token set; every animation names its job and has a reduced-motion form."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Accent Means Act Rule",
        "body": "Teal appears only on things you can press, the thing that is selected, or progress you caused. Never on decoration, headings or charts that are not ReSauce's own method.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Colour Alone Rule",
        "body": "Orange-red is always paired with the filled diamond symbol and a word (\"Discrepancy\", \"Discrepancy to review\"). A red element without its symbol and word is a bug.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measure Not Boxes Rule",
        "body": "Reading text is held to 68ch (`--measure`); hierarchy is made with size and weight, not extra containers.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Copyable Is Mono Rule",
        "body": "IDs, dates, offsets and counts set in Plex Mono at 0.92em; words never do.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Floaters Lift Rule",
        "body": "A surface carries the shadow only if it sits above the page (the focused review card, a dialog). Cards in the flow stay flat with a border.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every duration and curve from the motion tokens (fast 150ms, base 200ms, slow 250ms, layout 320ms; ease-out to enter, ease-in to leave, ease-move to travel in place; 18ms stagger) and say in a comment what job the motion does (orient, guide attention, show progress, connect cause and effect).",
      "**Do** give every movement a reduced-motion form that keeps the information as an opacity or colour change, via the token overrides or `lib/motion.js`.",
      "**Do** use the sign component for any new status, with an icon, a word and at most one colour.",
      "**Do** keep the synthetic-data banner on every page.",
      "**Do** set dark-theme values in both the system-preference block and the `data-theme=\"dark\"` block."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** show discrepancy, or any status, by colour alone.",
      "**Don't** use teal for anything that cannot be acted on or is not selected.",
      "**Don't** add bounce, shake or spring curves; entering eases out, leaving eases in.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to in-flow cards; use the border.",
      "**Don't** add KPI tiles or headline numbers; every figure on screen comes from the pipeline, results files or docs."
    ]
  }
}
